\description{
Makes the cohort's experimental design from its samples, in the Cohort view, before any comparison of groups: the replicate unit (a field naming each biological replicate, such as subject), the field whose groups are compared and its reference level, the contrasts (each level against the reference if not given), covariates (fields, or the bundles' run, slide and panel: numbers as they are, text as factors) and samples left out with their reasons. A unit's samples in one group are technical replicates, combined into one row; a unit in more than one group pairs them (the units enter the model). Answers the design in words, its rows (units in groups, with their samples), its matrix's columns (treatment coding, as patsy's) and rows, its rank and residual degrees of freedom, the contrasts, the samples left out, notes, and, when it cannot be used, why: a group of fewer than two units, regions of one section as separate units (unless pseudo_samples, for teaching), a term confounded with another, no degrees of freedom left, or the groups confounded with a slide, run or panel. With save, keeps it in the project as a new version of that name. Without a unit or group, answers the latest saved design.
